*Basic set relations.** `A ⊆ B` means every element of `A` lies in `B`;
`A = B` is equivalent to mutual inclusion `A ⊆ B` and `B ⊆ A`; and
`A ⊂ B` (proper subset) is equivalent to `A ⊆ B` together with `A ≠ B`.
